            <div xml:id="d423">

                <pb facs="0555" n="543" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg543"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/6181: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-22T10:00:00+02:00">October 22,
                            1940—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 22—8:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1004. My 1001, October 21, 9 p.m. Substantially identical information has been
                    given one of our correspondents by a high German Embassy official who intimated
                    that Italian attack this week would be on a relatively small scale for purpose
                    of testing Greek temper and resistance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
